@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il03-nouns`

-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version] s 164 and the Income Tax (Deduction from Salary and Wages)
-- Regulations 5753-1993 (withholding from an employee's pay).
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Sources, both deposited under ../../registers/source-bundle/ and both UNOFFICIAL Hebrew Wikisource
-- consolidations (raw MediaWiki):
--   the Ordinance   income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt  sha256 b87f2cf4...6b81b6 (s 164 is lines 5322-5323)
--   the Regulations regulations/income-tax-deduction-from-salary-and-wages-regulations-5753-1993.he.wiki.txt
--                   sha256 e6fd6975...b7b20f (retrieved 2026-10-08, Wikisource revision 2987411)
-- A `src:N` comment quotes line N of the Regulations file (or, in the s 164 module, of the Ordinance
-- file), copied mechanically; nothing in Hebrew here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is new Israeli shekels (NIS), a bare NUMBER. The tax year is the calendar year of the payment.
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the fact, or the
-- employee's card (form 0101) records it. What the fact does to the tax is a rule, and belongs in a rules module.

§ `Nouns for section 164 and the Deduction from Salary and Wages Regulations`

§§ `The kinds of payment on which section 164 imposes a duty to deduct`

-- Section 164 lists what the payer deducts tax from. The list is closed except for the last item, which
-- the Minister of Finance may extend by order with the approval of the Knesset Finance Committee.
DECLARE `A kind of payment named in section 164` IS ONE OF
    `employment income, including the part of a retirement or death grant not exempt under section 9(7A)` -- הכנסת עבודה
    `winnings or profit from gambling, lotteries or prize-bearing activity, as in section 2A`
    `an amount received on the capitalisation of a pension that is not exempt under section 9A or 9B`
    `amounts and payments to which section 18(b) applies and that are income in the recipient's hands`
    `income under section 2(5)`
    `amounts and payments to which section 3(e7) applies`
    `taxable income a real estate investment fund passes to its shareholders, as in section 64A2`
    `consideration within the meaning of section 88`
    `interest or dividend`
    `any other income the Minister of Finance has fixed by order, with the approval of the Knesset Finance Committee`

§§ `The readings of the four forks (version 0.1.0)`

-- Where the text is silent and the readings give different answers, the reading is a switch: ruled by Meng on
-- 2026-10-08 (SHRUG), one named switch for each, declined by default where the readings part, every other
-- reading kept by name. A reading is an argument of a rule, never a field of the case records.
--
-- Fork F1. Schedule A item (3) takes the credit points into account "from the tax so computed"; item (2) says
-- the tax so computed is the tax under ss 121 AND 121B. The Ordinance (s 33A) sets a credit point off against
-- the tax for the year. Whether the additional tax of s 121B can be reduced by credit points is the question.
DECLARE `A reading of Schedule A on what the credit points are set off against` IS ONE OF
    `against the whole of the tax computed under sections 121 and 121B`
    `against the section 121 tax only, never below nil, the section 121B tax added after`
    `declined where the object of the set-off changes the tax`        -- the default

-- Fork F2. Item (5) rounds a fraction of a shekel "from the salary or from the tax" and does not say whether
-- the salary is rounded before item (1) multiplies it, or only the tax at the end.
DECLARE `A reading of Schedule A item (5) on when the salary is rounded` IS ONE OF
    `the salary is rounded before it is multiplied by 12`
    `the salary is multiplied by 12 as it stands and only the tax is rounded`
    `declined where the order of rounding changes the tax`           -- the default

-- Fork F3. Regulation 3(b) deducts, on each part of a month's salary, "a proportionate part" of the tax on the
-- month's salary, and does not say whether that share is rounded to the shekel.
DECLARE `A reading of regulation 3(b) on rounding the share of the tax on a part` IS ONE OF
    `the share is rounded as item (5) of Schedule A rounds a tax`
    `the share is exact`
    `declined where rounding the share changes the tax`              -- the default

-- Fork F4. Schedule A computes the tax "under ss 121 and 121B, taking into account the necessary adjustments from
-- s 120B", and s 120B adjusts the amounts on 1 January of each tax year. The Regulations do not say which year's
-- amounts a payment is deducted by when the salary is for one tax year and is paid in the next (a December salary
-- paid in January): the year of the payment, or the year of the work. (Regulation 12(b) treats a payment made
-- between 1 and 13 January for an earlier tax year as paid in that earlier year, but only for the report.)
DECLARE `A reading of which tax year's amounts a payment is deducted by` IS ONE OF
    `the year in which the salary is paid`
    `the year for which the salary is paid`
    `declined where the year changes the tax`                         -- the default

§§ `The readings, together`

-- `placing` and `age` are the readings of IL-03's forks F1 and F2 (s 121(b)(1)), which the section 121 tax
-- of a salary passes through unchanged. The withholding rules add the three above.
DECLARE `The readings of the withholding rules` HAS
    `the set-off`  IS A `A reading of Schedule A on what the credit points are set off against`
    `the salary`   IS A `A reading of Schedule A item (5) on when the salary is rounded`
    `the share`    IS A `A reading of regulation 3(b) on rounding the share of the tax on a part`
    `the amounts`  IS A `A reading of which tax year's amounts a payment is deducted by`
    `the placing`  IS A `A reading of section 121(b)(1) on where the eligible income sits on the scale`
    `the age`      IS A `A reading of section 121(b)(1) on when the age of 60 is tested`

§§ `The annual figures the Regulations take from elsewhere`

-- Schedule A computes tax "under ss 121 and 121B, taking into account the necessary adjustments from s 120B"
-- and sets off credit points. The amounts that result for a tax year are s 120B's work (row IL-03 for the
-- income ceilings, row IL-01 for the credit point), and the Regulations do not print them. Both are inputs
-- with no default; ito-il26-published-figures.l4 records what the Israel Tax Authority published, not law.
DECLARE `The annual figures for the tax year` HAS
    `the amount in section 121B(a) in force in the tax year` IS A NUMBER
    `the value of one credit point`                           IS A NUMBER

§§ `What the employee declares`

-- Regulation 2: the employee's card (form 0101), filled in within a week of starting work and on 1 January
-- each year; and regulation 5(c): form 0130, a declaration that the partial salary, pension or wages are the
-- employee's only taxable income. The credit points are those the employee claims on the card, in
-- accordance with Schedule A item (3); who is entitled to how many is the business of ss 34 to 40D and 66(c)
-- of the Ordinance (rows IL-01, IL-02, IL-08), and is an input here.
DECLARE `The employee's declarations` HAS
    `gave the employer an employee's card (form 0101)`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `filled in the section of the card on other income`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared on the card an additional position, or a taxable pension from another payer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared on form 0130 that there is no other taxable income`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `told the employer of other taxable income after making that declaration`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `credit points claimed on the card`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `date of birth`                                                                       IS A DATE

§§ `The payment`

-- One payment of salary by one employer to one employee. Dates and hours are the facts the definitions of
-- regulation 1 turn on: "עובד יומי" (fewer than 18 days in the month, but not fewer than 8 hours a week),
-- "משכורת חלקית" (5 hours a day or fewer, or more than 5 hours a day but fewer than 8 hours a week),
-- "משכורת חודש" (work of a month, not fewer than 18 days), "משכורת בעד משרה נוספת" (more than 5 hours a day,
-- employed elsewhere or receiving a taxable pension from another payer).
DECLARE `A payment of salary` HAS
    `tax year`                                                                   IS A NUMBER  -- the year in which the salary is paid
    `the tax year for which the salary is paid`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `the month's salary`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the part of the month's salary paid in this payment`                        IS A NUMBER
    `days worked in the month`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `hours worked a day`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `hours worked a week`                                                        IS A NUMBER
    `the payment is a pension`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is a foreign worker`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee works elsewhere, or receives a taxable pension from another payer` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A non-regular salary (regulation 4(a)): paid on top of, or apart from, the month's salary.
DECLARE `A non-regular salary` HAS
    `amount`                                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `paid to the employees of a bankrupt or a company in liquidation`              IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `How regulations 3 and 5 treat a payment`

-- The three ways the Regulations deduct from one payment of salary or pension that this row answers. The
-- remaining payments are declined by name in ito-il26-regulations.l4: a foreign worker (regulation 3(d),
-- Schedule C) and a day employee (regulation 3(c), Schedule B), which are outside this row's scope.
DECLARE `How regulations 3 and 5 treat a payment` IS ONE OF
    `a monthly salary: the tax of Schedule A`
    `a partial salary or a pension on the sole-income declaration: the tax of Schedule A`
    `deducted at the maximal rate`

§§ `The assessing officer's direction`

-- Regulations 4(c), 5(e)(1), 9(a) and 10: the assessing officer may direct the employer to reduce, avoid or
-- increase the deduction, and the employer must comply. The text does not say in what form a direction comes;
-- these are the three forms a deduction can take, ASSUMED, not read.
DECLARE `A direction of the assessing officer` IS ONE OF
    `no direction`
    `deduct nothing`
    `deduct at the rate`   HAS `the rate`             IS A NUMBER
    `deduct the amount`    HAS `the amount to deduct` IS A NUMBER

§§ `The grounds on which an employee may ask for a reduction (regulation 9(a))`

-- Source: see ito-il26-claims.l4 for the paragraph each ground is. One constructor for each of the 18 paragraphs that regulation 9(a) still prints
-- ((2) is repealed).
DECLARE `A ground for asking the assessing officer to reduce the deduction` IS ONE OF
    `blindness, or a disability of 100% or of 90% on the special computation (section 9(5))`
    `residence in a settlement or area given a benefit (sections 11, 11A, 11B or another law)`
    `being a new immigrant (section 35)`
    `marriage within the tax year (section 37)`
    `the work of an unregistered spouse (section 38), if a separate computation was not asked for`
    `maintenance paid to a former spouse after marrying another (section 40A)`
    `donations above the adjusted amount (section 46)`
    `the cost of keeping a relative in an institution (section 44)`
    `dependants without means (section 45)`
    `payments under section 45A or 47, or section 4 of the Income Tax Ordinance Amendment (No. 2) Law 5722-1962`
    `the birth of a child within the tax year, for a female employee (sections 40(b)(1) or 66(c)(3))`
    `a spouse of 16 but not 18 whom the employee supports (section 40B)`
    `payments for parallel tax or medical insurance (section 47A)`
    `credit points not given for want of income in part of the tax year`
    `the credit points of a discharged soldier (section 39A)`
    `credit points under section 40C or 40D`
    `membership or handling fees (Income Tax (Deduction of Certain Expenses) Regulations 5732-1972)`
    `professional liability insurance paid through the employer under a collective agreement`

§§ `Invalid input`

-- Invalid input is rejected, not answered (EITHER, left side): the caller can fix it.
DECLARE `A problem with the payment, for the withholding rules` IS ONE OF
    `an amount of salary is negative`
    `the credit points claimed are negative`
    `the part of the month's salary paid exceeds the month's salary`
    `a number of days or hours is negative`
